# Command linode-cli

## What does this command do:

The official Linode command line interface.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: pip install --user linode-cli

## Command path

For Fedora run: /home/kinscoe/.local/bin/linode-cli

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/linode/linode-cli

## Command options

# First-time configuration (browser OAuth flow)
linode-cli configure

# Configure with a Personal Access Token instead of browser
linode-cli configure --token

# Print version
linode-cli --version

# List all available commands
linode-cli --help

# Show help for a specific command (e.g. linodes)
linode-cli linodes --help

# List Linode instances
linode-cli linodes list

# View a single Linode
linode-cli linodes view <linode-id>

# Create a Linode
linode-cli linodes create --type g6-nanode-1 --region us-east --image linode/debian12 --label myhost --root_pass '<pw>'

# Reboot / shutdown / boot
linode-cli linodes reboot   <linode-id>
linode-cli linodes shutdown <linode-id>
linode-cli linodes boot     <linode-id>

# Delete a Linode
linode-cli linodes delete <linode-id>

# List domains and DNS records
linode-cli domains list
linode-cli domains records-list <domain-id>

# Object storage (S3-compatible)
linode-cli obj ls
linode-cli obj mb <bucket>
linode-cli obj put <file> <bucket>

# StackScripts, images, regions, types
linode-cli stackscripts list --is_public true
linode-cli images list
linode-cli regions list
linode-cli linodes types

# Output formats
linode-cli linodes list --json --pretty
linode-cli linodes list --text --delimiter ','
linode-cli linodes list --markdown
linode-cli --format 'id,label,status,region' linodes list

# Show all rows / all columns
linode-cli linodes list --all-rows --all-columns

# Run as a different configured user
linode-cli --as-user <username> linodes list

# Suppress warnings (for scripting)
linode-cli --suppress-warnings linodes list

# Aliases: linode-cli is also available as `lin` and `linode`
